# ReconForge Synthetic Dataset — Description

Generated by `generator.py`, seed `6643` (reproducible — rerunning produces
identical output). Sized and shaped per the ReconForge blueprint (Sections
9–12): a **historical** split for backtesting/policy evaluation, and a
**live** split that plays out a scripted incident narrative for the demo.

---

## 1. Files

```
reconforge_dataset/
├── historical_internal_ledger.csv / .json          8,000 records
├── historical_processor_settlement.csv / .json     8,115 records (includes duplicate injections)
├── historical_ground_truth.csv / .json             8,000 records — evaluator-only truth
├── live_internal_ledger.csv / .json                1,500 records
├── live_processor_settlement.csv / .json           1,500 records
├── live_ground_truth.csv / .json                   1,500 records — evaluator-only truth
├── incident_memories.csv                           4 seed long-term-memory entries
├── policy_v1.json                                  initial ACTIVE matching policy
├── candidate_policy_examples.json                  2 example evolved policies (v2, v3)
└── dataset_manifest.json                           run metadata (seed, sizes, phase boundaries)

ReconForge_Reconciliation_Dataset.zip               everything above, zipped
```

Both CSV and JSON are written for every table — use CSV for quick
inspection/Excel, JSON for loading straight into Mongo collections or
Python.

