## 8. What changed from the first version

| Issue | Before | Now |
|---|---|---|
| Join-key leak | `transaction_id` identical in both ledger and settlement records — trivial equi-join, no real matching required | Removed entirely from both tables; hidden key (`label_group_id`) lives only in ground truth |
| Customer matching | No `customer_id` field, but policy referenced `require_same_customer` | Added `customer_id` (400-value pool), wired into `policy_v1` |
| Units | Amounts as float dollars; policy said `amount_tolerance: 0.00` | Amounts as integer `amount_cents`; policy renamed to `amount_tolerance_cents`, matching the blueprint's Evolution-agent schema (0–25 range) |
| Demo trigger reliability | Fee/delay values drawn randomly per record — deterministic ">=70% same delta" trigger wasn't guaranteed to fire | `fee_drift` and `settlement_drift` phases now pin one processor + one fixed value each — verified 100% consistent |
| Stale files | Re-running with a changed schema could leave old files mixed into `reconforge_dataset/` and the zip | Output directory is now wiped before each run |

All other structural choices from the original script — the
historical/live split, three-phase live narrative, physical duplicate
injection, seeded memories, and candidate policies — are unchanged; they
were sound design decisions.

